@startuml
' OWNER-MVP-2026-11-04 review: MVP core / cross-cutting. Core presentation/application/files or shared authority/recovery invariant remains applicable.
title Proposed disaster recovery and optional standby gate
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial

start
:Identify failure / compromise and actual service/data scope;
:Restrict unsafe access; exclude competing writers / effects;
if (Evaluated standby actually exists?) then (yes)
 :Validate standby consistency / keys / current authority;\nverify fencing and routing prerequisites;
else (no — current design fact)
 if (Usable identified backup actually available?) then (yes)
  :Restore compatible protected set into isolated target;
 else (no / unknown)
  :Record unmet recovery prerequisite;\nretain safe state and assess actual recovery options;
  stop
 endif
endif
:Validate usable workflows / current access / external effects;\nrecord actual recoverable point, loss and elapsed time;
if (Reviewed promotion prerequisites satisfied?) then (yes)
 :Promote scoped target; guard writes / traffic / background resumption;
else (no / unknown)
 :Retain isolation; report real recovery limits and unresolved effects;
endif
stop
legend bottom
 No backup destination or standby is currently established by this project design.
 This is a recovery procedure, not installed automatic failover or an accepted RPO/RTO.
endlegend
@enduml
